# WP-8 part 1: the two manifest-detected reds for the never-written observation, with their ablation.
# Each root is an out-of-tree copy of the shared tree; the injection entry runs there, urg reports that root's own
# database, and ci/check_fcov_expectations.py reads the report with dv/auto_dv/fcov_expectations/gen_cg_ic_ecc_part1.fcov.yaml.
# Lines below are read from those runs' own files, not retyped, and ASCII-normalised per the retention convention
# (the em dash the checker prints becomes '-').
#
# READ THE DISCRIMINATION, NOT THE EXIT CODE. All three runs pass in simulation and the checker exits 2 in all three,
# because ONE run cannot hit all fifteen declared bins: no tag injection, no two-bit knob, no disabled-cache case and
# no invalidating case occur in it, which is why the manifest spans entries. The evidence is the named bin's
# transition from HIT to UNHIT, and the statistic that says WHICH half of the mechanism the mutation removed.

root: GREEN   (no mutation, the control)
  sources sha256: 61da6da315ee239e
  simulation verdict: PASS
  | uninitialised data reads reported=37 sampled=35 skipped(injection 2, alert 0) dropped=0
  | FCOV-EXPECTATION: gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.uninitialised_data_ram = HIT (count=35)
  | FCOV-EXPECTATION: FAIL - 5 declared bin(s) not hit: gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_ram.tag, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_bits.double, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.disabled_cache, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.during_invalidation, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.masked_duplicate_copy

root: UNINITALL   (the written flag set for every line at init, so no read is ever never-written)
  sources sha256: bf78b5c353a92660
  simulation verdict: PASS
  | uninitialised data reads reported=0 sampled=0 skipped(injection 0, alert 0) dropped=0
  | FCOV-EXPECTATION: gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.uninitialised_data_ram = UNHIT (count=0)
  | FCOV-EXPECTATION: FAIL - 6 declared bin(s) not hit: gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_ram.tag, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_bits.double, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.disabled_cache, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.during_invalidation, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.uninitialised_data_ram, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.masked_duplicate_copy

root: UNINITDRAIN   (both drain calls removed, so events are queued and never classified)
  sources sha256: 08e1f203a788b1f5
  simulation verdict: PASS
  | uninitialised data reads reported=37 sampled=0 skipped(injection 0, alert 0) dropped=0
  | FCOV-EXPECTATION: gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.uninitialised_data_ram = UNHIT (count=0)
  | FCOV-EXPECTATION: FAIL - 6 declared bin(s) not hit: gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_ram.tag, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_bits.double, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.disabled_cache, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.during_invalidation, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.uninitialised_data_ram, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.masked_duplicate_copy

# ABLATION, the same two reports with the bin removed from the manifest, so the detector is gone and nothing else changes:
UNINITALL ablation, exit 2
  | FCOV-EXPECTATION: FAIL - 5 declared bin(s) not hit: gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_ram.tag, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_bits.double, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.disabled_cache, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.during_invalidation, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.masked_duplicate_copy
  | the bin is named 0 times, so its appearance above is caused by the declaration plus the mutation

UNINITDRAIN ablation, exit 2
  | FCOV-EXPECTATION: FAIL - 5 declared bin(s) not hit: gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_ram.tag, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_bits.double, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.disabled_cache, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.during_invalidation, gen_ic_ecc_cg.cp_no_alert_case.masked_duplicate_copy
